### A book's own accessibility information (EPUB Accessibility metadata).

## Said after the document overview and printed by tw info for an EPUB,
## one fact per line, meaning first. The first line is one of the four
## leads; the details follow when the book gives them. $list is a list of
## terms in words ("table of contents, alternative text"), $text the
## publisher's own words, $name a certifier's name.
access-info-friendly = إمكانية الوصول: صديق لقارئ الشاشة، بحسب الناشر.
access-info-not-text = إمكانية الوصول: بعضه لا يُقرأ كنص، بحسب الناشر.
access-info-given = إمكانية الوصول: وصفها الناشر.
access-info-none = لا توجد معلومات عن إمكانية الوصول.
access-info-summary = الملخص: { $text }.
access-info-modes = أنماط الوصول: { $list }.
access-info-sufficient = يُقرأ بـ: { $list }.
access-info-features = الميزات: { $list }.
access-info-hazards = المخاطر: { $list }.
access-info-conformance = يتوافق مع: { $text }.
access-info-certifier = اعتمده: { $name }.
# Joins two sets of access modes in access-info-sufficient: "text, or text and images".
access-info-or = { $first }، أو { $second }
# Joins the access modes inside one set: "text and images".
access-info-and = { $first } و{ $second }
